2026-09-27T12:06:27.9512272Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9512549Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9513010Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9513443Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9513573Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9513873Z ================
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9514114Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9514344Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9514889Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9515211Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9515381Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9515782Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9516050Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9516251Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9516797Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9517677Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9518681Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9519654Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9519823Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9520491Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9521396Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9521873Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9522398Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9523107Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9523242Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9523547Z ========
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9523733Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9526036Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9528516Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9528906Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9529679Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9530869Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9531973Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9614685Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9615520Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9616312Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9616475Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9616830Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9617277Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9635018Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9636804Z 
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9638051Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9639398Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:06:27.9639718Z 
